From 70a9f7207c76c785f21b811e8c1398b2cb1ab2bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 23:11:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Real SMTP delivery, AI workflow fix, persisted failed runs,
 catch-up window

Email
- EMAIL_MODE=smtp: real delivery via SMTP_* (STARTTLS / SSL / none, optional
  login, certificate verification, no silent downgrade). "real" is an alias.
- One message per subscriber (was one shared message exposing every address).
- Drafts are marked sent/failed; re-running a newsletter never re-sends, and a
  partially failed run can be retried safely.
- mock mode is Mailpit only and ignores SMTP_* so it can never reach a provider.

AI workflow
- Set state.topic (was never assigned: every AI send failed "Topic not set").
- Score/generate from the scheduled article instead of re-fetching the topic.
- Low relevance routes to "skip" before any LLM generation.
- skipped / pending_review statuses are no longer overwritten with "sent".
- RELEVANCE_THRESHOLD env var is now honoured.

Scheduler
- Failed runs are persisted (savepoint per run) with the reason; one failing or
  malformed schedule no longer aborts or erases the rest of the scan.
- Each schedule is committed immediately and its window is claimed before
  sending, so a later error or a crash cannot cause a duplicate send.
- Catch-up window (SCHEDULE_CATCHUP_MINUTES, default 15) replaces exact-minute
  matching; window key is based on the scheduled moment.
- Run status reflects what actually happened (partial_failure,
  skipped_low_relevance, pending_review) instead of always "sent".
- Worker log now shows counts and failure reasons.

Tests: 26 new tests (SMTP via fake smtplib, workflow idempotency, scan
resilience, catch-up incl. midnight and DST gap, AI fixes); legacy exact-minute
assertions updated; RSS fixture dates made relative; conftest creates schema.
